{
  "ProgressBar shows how far some work is, as a line or a circle, or that it runs when that is not known. Spinner says \"busy, wait\": a turning ring, alone or over a panel while it loads, shown only after a delay so quick work does not flash it.": "",
  "Every prop takes a value or a function; a function of a reactive object keeps the bar in step with the work. Created with `new`, the same properties are set programmatically.": "",
  "Not known yet": "",
  "Without a value (`null`) the bar runs to and fro; give it a number once the work can tell how far it is.": "",
  "Line or circle": "",
  "`shape=\"circle\"` draws the progress as an arc that goes round a ring from the top; without a value the arc turns. The caption goes under it (`labelPosition=\"bottom\"`, its default), above it or beside it, and `size` sets the size of the circle and of its line. Where the design language gives it a wave (Material), the line and the arc swing while they grow, straight while little is done and again at the end.": "",
  "Sizes, caption beside, your own text": "",
  "`size` sets the thickness. `labelPosition=\"side\"` puts the label before the bar and the value after it. `valueText` writes the value its own way.": "",
  "Spinner": "",
  "A spinner with `delay` stays unseen for that long, from when it is created or shown again. Quick work shows nothing; slow work shows the spinner.": "",
  "Cover a panel while it loads": "",
  "`Spinner.cover(target)` lays a spinner over a component or an element and returns the function that takes it away. What is under it cannot be pressed or focused; focus that was inside waits on the spinner and comes back afterwards.": "",
  "`role=\"progressbar\"` with `aria-valuenow`, `aria-valuemin`, `aria-valuemax` and `aria-valuetext` (the percent or `valueText`); none of them while the progress is not known.": "",
  "`role=\"progressbar\"` without a value: an indicator of unknown progress, found and named like any widget. Not a `status` live region: those interrupt the reader each time one appears, and a page with many would be noisy.": "",
  "The label (`aria-labelledby`), or `uiLocale.strings.loading` when there is none.": "",
  "The container gets `aria-busy=\"true\"`; what is under the spinner is `inert`. Focus inside it moves to the spinner and comes back to where it was.": "",
  "With reduced motion the bar rests as a tinted track, a new value is shown at once, a wave keeps still, and the arcs, the ring and the shape stand still. A wave is drawn only while the bar is in sight.": "",
  "A bar or a spinner without a label is named `uiLocale.strings.loading`. The percent is written in `locale`, by default the page's `lang`.": "",
  "The bar. `data-state=\"determinate | indeterminate\"`, `data-complete`, `data-shape`, `data-wave` (a wave is drawn), `data-tone`, `data-size`, `data-label-position`, `data-stretch`; `--_fraction`: how much is done, 0 to 1.": "",
  "The caption row.": "",
  "The line: the track (`::before`: the rest of it, `::after`: the stop dot) and the part done (`::after`: the runner).": "",
  "The wave drawn over the track instead of the bar.": "",
  "The circle: its drawing, the ring and the arc.": "",
  "The spinner. `data-size`, `data-tone`, `data-label-position`, `data-contained`, `data-waiting`, `data-cover`.": "",
  "The container of what turns.": "",
  "The ring, the shape (the language shows one of them) and the label.": "",
  "A container under `Spinner.cover`.": "",
  "Units of the line, each with its box: the band, the part done, the rest of the track, the stop dot, the runner, the wave (its colour). States: `indeterminate`, `complete`, the tones.": "",
  "Units of the circle and of the caption.": "",
  "The line per size, the gap after the part done, the dot.": "",
  "The wave: how far it swings (0: none), how long a wave is and how fast and which way it travels, between which shares of the work it swings, how long it takes to grow in.": "",
  "The circle per size, its gaps, its turning arc and its wave.": "",
  "The width when not stretched, the caption, the tones.": "",
  "The ring and the shape per size.": "",
  "Units: the container (`contained`), the ring and the shape, each with its box.": "",
  "The shapes the shape becomes in turn (names from the shapes of the kit), how long the round takes, how each is reached, and one turn.": "",
  "Between the ring and the label.": "",
  "The layer over a covered container.": "",
  "ProgressBar props": "",
  "How far the work is. `null` (or no value) when that is not known: the bar runs to and fro, a circle turns.": "",
  "The bounds of `value`.": "",
  "A caption; it names the bar. The same property as `text`.": "",
  "`line`: a bar along a track; `circle`: an arc that goes round a ring from the top.": "",
  "`'top'` (`'bottom'` for a circle)": "",
  "`top`: the label and the value above the bar; `bottom`: under it; `side`: the label before it, the value after it.": "",
  "Writes the percent (whole, rounded down) or `valueText`.": "",
  "The text for a value, shown and read out (`3 of 12 files`). A function, so it is stored as it is, not bound.": "",
  "The locale of the percent.": "",
  "The thickness, and the size of a circle: `sm`, `md`, `lg`.": "",
  "Spinner props": "",
  "Text next to the ring. The same property as `text`.": "",
  "After the ring or under it.": "",
  "The color of the turning part.": "",
  "Inside a container of its own (a disc behind it), where the design language draws one.": "",
  "Milliseconds before it shows, from when it is created or shown again; quick work then shows nothing.": "",
  "Showing it again (`visible`) starts the delay again.": "",
  "Properties and methods": "",
  "Access / returns": "",
  "How much is done, from 0 to 1; `null` while it is not known.": "",
  "Still inside its delay.": "",
  "Covers a component or an element with a spinner; call the returned function to take it away. See Cover.": ""
}
